# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. wrangler auto-loads .env and uses
# these for its own authentication.

# Scoped Cloudflare API token for deploys/migrations. Preferred over the
# interactive `wrangler login` OAuth session: it never expires/refreshes, is
# headless/CI-friendly, and authenticates via /user/tokens/verify (a
# user-scoped endpoint that stays available during Cloudflare account-services
# / dashboard incidents — unlike OAuth, which resolves the account through the
# /accounts endpoint that those incidents take down).
#
# Create it: Cloudflare dashboard -> My Profile -> API Tokens -> Create Token
#   -> "Edit Cloudflare Workers" template, then under Account Resources
#   restrict to "Nmarkspdx@gmail.com's Account" only, and add the
#   "Account : D1 : Edit" permission (the template covers Workers but not D1).
# Minimum permissions for this repo:
#   Account : Workers Scripts : Edit
#   Account : D1 : Edit
#   Account : Account Settings : Read
#   Account : Workers Tail : Read   (used by `wrangler tail`)
# Scope it to account f8d78ce7cbf48da4f2a3ac9d9a63a5d5 only; no zone access needed.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
